Value Required PEER_ADDRESS ([^,\s]+)
Value PEER_AS (\d+)
Value LINK (external|internal)
Value DESCRIPTION (.+)
Value PEER_ROUTER_ID (\S+)
Value VRF (\S+)
Value PEER_GROUP (\S+)
Value STATE (\w+)
Value SHUTDOWN (Administratively shut down)
Value List NEGOTIATED (.+?)
Value LOCAL_AS (\d+)
Value ROUTER_ID (\S+)

# One record per peer, every VRF (feature 010, research R1). The Local AS line comes after the
# statistics blocks, so a record ends at the next "BGP neighbor is" or at the end of the output.
# Timers, counters, prefix statistics and TCP socket lines are never captured (FR-007).
Start
  ^BGP neighbor is -> Continue.Record
  ^BGP neighbor is ${PEER_ADDRESS}, remote AS ${PEER_AS}, ${LINK} link
  ^\s+Description: ${DESCRIPTION}$$
  ^\s+BGP version \d+, remote router ID ${PEER_ROUTER_ID}, VRF ${VRF}$$
  ^\s+Inherits configuration from and member of peer-group ${PEER_GROUP}$$
  ^\s+BGP state is ${STATE}, ${SHUTDOWN}$$
  ^\s+BGP state is ${STATE}
  # Only a family the session negotiated: once it is down EOS prints "advertised and received".
  ^\s+Multiprotocol ${NEGOTIATED}: .*\bnegotiated$$
  ^Local AS is ${LOCAL_AS}, local router ID ${ROUTER_ID}
